From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Subject: b43: HT-PHY: fill in the transmitter address of the BlockAck template

With an RX block ack session (the HT20 patch, ht_rx_ampdu=1) the ucode answers
each A-MPDU and BlockAckReq with a BlockAck built from template RAM. The
driver has to write the station's own MAC address into that template at
offset 0x48 (T_BA_TPL_BASE + 16), as brcmsmac's brcms_c_ampdu_macaddr_upd()
does. b43 never wrote it, so every BlockAck went out with TA
00:00:00:00:00:00 (seen on an ath11k monitor: 2139 such BAs in 5 s). The
originator cannot match them, retransmits every A-MPDU, falls back to
MCS 0 and sends BARs: a thin uplink stream such as TCP ACKs collapsed the
download to ~2.3 Mbit/s, while the bulk upload hid it behind duplicates.

Write the TA together with the MAC/BSSID templates on the HT-PHY.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index 2d05ff9..fabfc46 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -735,9 +735,26 @@ static void b43_write_mac_bssid_templates(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 	}
 }
 
+/* The ucode answers an A-MPDU with a BlockAck built from a template whose
+ * transmitter address the driver has to fill in (brcmsmac:
+ * brcms_c_ampdu_macaddr_upd). Without it the BlockAck goes out with
+ * TA 00:00:00:00:00:00 and the originator ignores it. */
+#define B43_TPL_BA_TA		0x48
+
+static void b43_write_ba_template_ta(struct b43_wldev *dev)
+{
+	const u8 *mac = dev->wl->mac_addr;
+
+	b43_ram_write(dev, B43_TPL_BA_TA, mac[0] | (mac[1] << 8) |
+		      (mac[2] << 16) | ((u32)mac[3] << 24));
+	b43_ram_write(dev, B43_TPL_BA_TA + 4, mac[4] | (mac[5] << 8));
+}
+
 static void b43_upload_card_macaddress(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
 	b43_write_mac_bssid_templates(dev);
+	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
+		b43_write_ba_template_ta(dev);
 	b43_macfilter_set(dev, B43_MACFILTER_SELF, dev->wl->mac_addr);
 }
 
